# LazyLabelText — example .env file
#
# COPY this file to ".env" (in the same folder, or wherever you point the
# loader at via Provider Settings → "Load .env file at startup") and fill in
# the credentials for whichever provider(s) you actually use. Lines that
# start with # are comments and are ignored.
#
# IMPORTANT:
#   - Never commit a real .env (the project's .gitignore already blocks .env
#     and .env.* — only .env.example is tracked).
#   - The loader does NOT overwrite values that are already in your shell
#     environment, so a real `export` always wins.
#   - The loader is read once at app launch (and again when you save
#     Provider Settings).


# ─── Anthropic (Claude) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx


# ─── OpenAI (non-Azure) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# Used by the OpenAI LLM provider AND the OpenAI embedding provider
# (text-embedding-ada-002 / text-embedding-3-small / text-embedding-3-large).
#
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx


# ─── Google Gemini ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=AIzaSyxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx


# ─── Azure OpenAI ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# https://portal.azure.com → your AOAI resource → Keys and Endpoint
# Required for the "azure" LLM and embedding providers. The api_version is
# also configurable per-session in Provider Settings; OPENAI_API_VERSION
# is the env-var fallback when that field is left blank.
#
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=your-32-char-azure-key
# AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=https://your-resource.openai.azure.com
# OPENAI_API_VERSION=2024-08-01-preview


# ─── Tiktoken offline cache (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Set this if you've copied a `cl100k_base.tiktoken` file to a non-default
# location and want structural chunking to use it without internet.
#
# TIKTOKEN_CACHE_DIR=/path/to/your/tiktoken/cache


# Tip: most users only fill in ONE LLM provider section + (optionally) one
# embedding provider. Leave the rest commented out.
